# PostgreSQL 18 + pgvector 0.8.6 + Apache AGE 1.8.0: the "one engine" rival to
# the cross-model transaction (pgvector hit, Cypher hop through AGE, row update,
# one transaction). Base image pinned by digest; AGE from the PGDG apt repo the
# postgres image already carries. Built as dbbench:pg-age by build_images.sh.
#
# MOVED TO PG18 ON 2026-09-19 WITH THE REST OF THE POSTGRESQL SET (DECISIONS
# #87, #103d: one engine wears one version per page). postgres, pgvector and
# TimescaleDB moved to their pg18 builds in the same commit, and THIS image is
# the one that gated the set: AGE is the only one of the four packaged per
# PostgreSQL major, so the set could only move once PGDG carried an AGE build
# for 18. It does -- 1.8.0~rc0 on apt.postgresql.org, bookworm and trixie --
# and the extension version is read back onto the row at connect, so the row
# records what was installed rather than what this file asked for.
#
# BOTH AGE ENDPOINTS ARE ~rc0 DEBIAN PACKAGES, and that is not a regression:
# the PG17 pin this replaces was 1.7.0~rc0. Apache AGE tags every release -rc0
# and votes that artifact through as the release, so there is no non-rc build
# to pin to and "latest stable" for AGE means the newest -rc0 for the major.
FROM pgvector/pgvector@sha256:1d50c689b0a6511b9ea0a15615281c81a59fd04a08eb35057ec8646fb3a2118a
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends postgresql-18-age \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*
